        <body>
            <div xml:id="d826">

                <pb facs="0972" n="878" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg878"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terrell to Mr.
                            Olney.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-01-11"><hi rendition="#italic">January 11, 1897</hi></date>.
                        (Received Jan. 25.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1135.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that
                    Missionary Cole, at Bitlis, telegraphed me requesting the withdrawal of the
                    Turkish guard at that place. I have had telegraphic orders sent complying with
                    his request as you were informed by telegram, a copy of which I append on the
                    overleaf.</p>
                <p>No reasons were given by Mr. Cole for wishing to dispense with a guard.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. W. Terrell.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
